---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DiscordSummary from '../components/DiscordSummary.svelte';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ThreadArchive from '../components/ThreadArchive.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import config from '../config.json';

// Nothing here is per-request: the island fetches /api/discord-summary in the browser, and the rest
// of the page is static markup. Prerendering turns /chat into a static asset (no Worker CPU, no cold
// start, edge-cacheable) - verified: `dist/client/chat/index.html` appears in the build output.
export const prerender = true;

// One place for the invite, because the island's empty and failed states need to offer the same
// path out that the CTA does (D108: a designed state names where the content lives) — and the footer
// band names the same destination. That one place is `URLs.discordInvite` in src/config.json.
const DISCORD_URL = config.URLs.discordInvite;
// The list itself is a component now (S089, D465): it reads the ratified archive in
// `data/discord-threads.json`, and everything that decides what a visitor may see about the club's own
// conversations lives beside the rule that checks it. This page places the section and keeps the anchor the
// home page promises; it no longer holds the list's source. `src/lib/threads-view.mjs`'s `publishedThreads()` is
// the one view, so the page cannot print an evidence field it was not handed.
---

<Layout title="Chat - Matheapolis, a Minneapolis math club" path="/chat">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-8">
    {/* No eyebrow above the h1 (S040, second design read §1, 2026-11-14): the page's name is its h1, and the
        line under it says what the page holds. "Community Chat" above the heading was a locator the nav already
        supplies - `check:naming` (D309) holds nav, title, band and heading to one word, and the new rule in the
        same gate fails any text between `<main>` and the first heading. The air is unchanged: mb-4 + mb-8 is
        the same 48px the h1's mb-12 spent, and both steps are on DESIGN.md's ladder — `mb-10` (40px) was not,
        and `npm run check:scale` (S042, D321) now fails any spacing write off it. */}
    {/* Round-6 review (2026-11-16), `/chat`/Revise (D409): "The page is named for a thing that isn't on it."
        The h1 used to read "Summaries from the chat" and the section under it - the bot's reading - is what
        the server renders as a notice with nothing under it, so the page promised summaries it did not carry.
        The name now says what the page is: the club's chat. The bot keeps its own heading **inside the island**
        (see `DiscordSummary.svelte`), on the branch that has content under it, and the pending branch becomes
        a warm static state instead of a heading over a void (D409). `check:naming`'s `name-not-on-page` is
        still satisfied: the nav word is "Chat", and the h1 says it. The subtitle carries the page's three
        holdings in words rather than naming only the one section that may be empty, and it says them in words
        that do not restate the thread lead below it: `check:content`'s `near-duplicate-surface` fired on a
        subtitle sharing "where the club talks" with that lead, which is the same sentence of the same page
        printed in two surfaces (D273's rule: shared words across surfaces is a defect unless a ruling says the
        repeat is the point, and here it is not the point - the two lines answer different questions). */}
    <h1 class="text-display-1 font-extrabold text-ink mb-4">
      The club’s chat
    </h1>
    {/* Round-8 review (2026-11-18), `/chat`/Revise: "Lede promises 'the dates the club set' — the page
        contains no dates. Delete those four words, or add the two upcoming dates." The four words are deleted
        rather than the dates added: `/chat` is not the page of record for dates, and D218 keeps dates on the
        surfaces its `RULED` map names, so a fourth date-bearing surface is the defect `check-dated-surfaces`
        exists to catch. The subtitle now names the two things this page does hold. */}
    <p class="text-label uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-3 mb-8">The live channel, and the threads worth reading</p>

    {/* A3 (round-5 communication read, 2026-11-16, D367): the page's ONE way out used to sit 1,720px down at
        1240 and y=2,075 at 390 — a phone visitor scrolled two screens of prose before reaching the only action
        `/chat` offers, which the read called the worst communication defect on the artifact. So the invite the
        page already owns moves UP into the first screen as a declared control: `data-control="secondary"`, the
        ratified secondary construction (paper fill, `inset-shadow-rule`, `text-label`, 48px — D139's single
        pressable step, D140's declared role), on `paper` and not inside a tinted card or a notice (D149-3c's
        one-boundary rule, which `check:render` enforces as "a notice contains a block action"). It reuses
        `config.URLs.discordInvite` — the one home for the invite, named in the comment above — so R1's ceiling
        moves from 2 outbound anchors outside the band to 3, under the cap of 6 that `check:rsvp-page` prints,
        and `check:ext-links` still sees a qualifier on it. The CTA below keeps its words and its role: this is
        the same path met earlier, which is why it is a secondary and not a second primary — "a band with two
        primaries has no primary" (Schedule.astro's own note). */}
    {/* MS41 (S090, D467): the control is the same one D367 moved up, with the same words, the same secondary
        construction and the same sr-only qualifier — and now it carries the sentence the operator's complaint
        said was missing. "Join the chat" alone hides what the click does: Discord's own Invite Object is "a code
        that when used, adds a user to a guild" @retrieved 2026-11-20 from
        https://discord.com/developers/docs/resources/invite, so the ask is joining a **server**, and the sentence
        under the control says so. It is printed from `CALL_TO_ACTION['discord-server'].says` in
        `src/lib/links.mjs`, not typed here, and `data-cta-block="discord-server"` is what
        `scripts/check-cta-context.mjs` reads — so the page and the gate cannot be edited apart. */}
    <CallToAction
      id="discord-server"
      role="secondary"
      href={DISCORD_URL}
      label="Join the chat"
      gloss
      wrap="mt-8"
    />

    {/* `visible`, not `load`: the summary block is below the fold on phones, and this island
         drags in ~34 KB of Svelte runtime plus its own 3.8 KB. Hydrating on visibility leaves the
         server-rendered heading and the "Join the chat" CTA interactive immediately and skips
         the API fetch entirely for visitors who never scroll to it.
         Round-8 review (2026-11-18), `/chat`/Revise "move 'No summary written this week' to the end… a
        scanner's first impression is that nothing is here": the island moves BELOW the thread list, so the
        page's first screen carries the list the visitor can act on and the bot's section — the only part
        that can be empty — is last, one quiet line above the band. Nothing about the island itself changed:
        same component, same `visible` hydration, same states. */}

    {/* The threads, in full, from the ratified archive (S042 -> S089, D465). The section keeps its shape and its
        anchor: `id="threads"` is where the home page's "the rest of the list ->" lands, and `check:threads`'s
        `dead-anchor` rule fails a promise that lands nowhere (D273's class). What is under the anchor changed on
        2026-11-20: nine subjects an agent wrote down from memory became 31 topics harvested off two years of the
        club's channels, each one signed by the operator and traceable to messages (**D461**, **D464**). The
        section lives in its own component now, with its source, its order, and the rule that keeps evidence off
        the page. */}
    <ThreadArchive />

    {/* Round-8 review (2026-11-18), `/chat`/Revise: "'The channel is the live thing' appears three times…
        Cut lines 37-40 entirely — 'The chat itself' says nothing the first two didn't." The section is deleted,
        not reworded, and with it goes the sentence that was this page talking about itself.
        What the deletions in this card were for, kept so the next read does not re-derive it: D414 deleted a
        clause that claimed summaries sat above, D437 deleted the card's own Discord control rather than the
        fold secondary (deleting that one instead would return `/chat` to D367's measured defect — the page's
        one way out 1,720px down at 1240 and at y=2,075 at 390), and both left `/chat` painting ONE pressable
        Discord control plus the band's link, which is the count `check:rsvp-page` prints as 1 outside the band
        against the ceiling of 6 D358 ratified. Deleting the card moves no anchor and adds no URL. */}

    <DiscordSummary client:visible discordUrl={DISCORD_URL} />
  </main>
  {/* Every page the build emits closes with the exit band (D115, enforced by check:page-exit). This page has
     one island and one CTA; without the band a visitor who arrives here from a shared link has the nav above
     and nothing below. */}
  <Footer />
</Layout>
